1
00:01:50,040 --> 00:01:50,280
Dad,

2
00:01:50,560 --> 00:01:50,920
go ahead.

3
00:01:51,560 --> 00:01:53,480
Well, in our construction team,

4
00:01:53,480 --> 00:01:54,879
there's a fitter.

5
00:01:55,719 --> 00:01:56,920
He came down with...

6
00:01:58,599 --> 00:02:00,000
prostate...

7
00:02:01,079 --> 00:02:01,439
cancer.

8
00:02:01,760 --> 00:02:02,719
The hospital—

9
00:02:03,040 --> 00:02:04,920
one minute they say it's mid-stage,

10
00:02:04,920 --> 00:02:06,200
the next they say it's late-stage.

11
00:02:07,120 --> 00:02:08,039
Seeing him,

12
00:02:08,319 --> 00:02:08,919
he...

13
00:02:09,599 --> 00:02:10,599
he's really suffering.

14
00:02:10,680 --> 00:02:11,759
So I just wanted to ask...

15
00:02:12,080 --> 00:02:13,000
with this kind of thing,

16
00:02:13,479 --> 00:02:15,280
how... how do you handle it?

17
00:02:15,919 --> 00:02:18,319
Has he been to our hospital for a checkup?

18
00:02:18,919 --> 00:02:20,080
Our hospital is Honggang's

19
00:02:20,199 --> 00:02:21,159
biggest Grade-A tertiary hospital.

20
00:02:21,680 --> 00:02:22,919
The exams here are very comprehensive,

21
00:02:22,919 --> 00:02:24,080
and my colleagues in diagnostics

22
00:02:24,080 --> 00:02:25,639
are really dedicated and thorough.

23
00:02:26,080 --> 00:02:27,680
I'd suggest coming to our hospital soon

24
00:02:27,840 --> 00:02:28,840
for a full checkup.

25
00:02:29,800 --> 00:02:30,919
Otherwise, if he keeps putting it off,

26
00:02:33,199 --> 00:02:34,000
he'll only feel worse.

27
00:02:35,319 --> 00:02:35,599
Dad...

28
00:02:39,039 --> 00:02:39,479
are you...

29
00:02:40,840 --> 00:02:42,120
feeling bad right now?

30
00:02:45,039 --> 00:02:46,280
Why would I feel bad?

31
00:02:46,719 --> 00:02:48,039
It's not like I'm the one who's sick.

32
00:02:48,360 --> 00:02:48,639
No...

33
00:02:48,759 --> 00:02:49,639
I—I meant,

34
00:02:50,039 --> 00:02:50,879
are you...

35
00:02:51,319 --> 00:02:52,319
feeling bad for him?

36
00:02:53,280 --> 00:02:53,560
Dad,

37
00:02:53,919 --> 00:02:54,639
if anything comes up,

38
00:02:55,439 --> 00:02:56,840
call me anytime.

39
00:02:57,639 --> 00:02:58,919
I know, I know.

40
00:03:06,960 --> 00:03:08,319
Up late in the middle of the night,

41
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:10,479
talking about treating a worker.

42
00:03:12,159 --> 00:03:14,039
You're just born to worry.

43
00:03:17,759 --> 00:03:18,159
I'm...

44
00:03:18,680 --> 00:03:19,520
heading to the bathroom.

45
00:03:20,800 --> 00:03:21,240
All right.

46
00:03:21,599 --> 00:03:22,080
Be right back.

47
00:03:24,360 --> 00:03:24,879
Hurry up.

48
00:03:42,400 --> 00:03:44,360
My period's a few days late.

49
00:03:44,520 --> 00:03:45,479
My stomach hurts so bad right now.

50
00:03:45,719 --> 00:03:46,800
Are you at the hospital?

51
00:03:59,879 --> 00:04:00,840
I'm heading back to work.

52
00:04:01,080 --> 00:04:02,360
A heart attack patient just came into the ER.

53
00:04:05,560 --> 00:04:06,919
Didn't you just get home?

54
00:04:06,919 --> 00:04:08,000
Why are you leaving again?

55
00:04:08,280 --> 00:04:09,560
Isn't anyone on duty today?

56
00:04:09,960 --> 00:04:11,599
It's the doctor on duty who called me.

57
00:04:11,840 --> 00:04:12,599
He can't handle it.

58
00:04:12,879 --> 00:04:13,919
So I have to go in.

59
00:04:15,520 --> 00:04:16,079
Don't worry.

60
00:04:16,319 --> 00:04:16,959
I'll be back soon.

61
00:04:17,879 --> 00:04:18,279
Besides,

62
00:04:18,680 --> 00:04:20,360
I'm the department's only deputy director.

63
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:21,800
If I don't step up,

64
00:04:22,480 --> 00:04:23,319
who's gonna promote me?

65
00:04:23,519 --> 00:04:23,920
Right?

66
00:04:25,319 --> 00:04:25,879
I'll be right back.

67
00:04:27,600 --> 00:04:27,920
Wait for me.

68
00:04:32,360 --> 00:04:33,839
Come back early, then.

69
00:04:34,040 --> 00:04:35,160
Don't wear yourself out.

70
00:04:36,120 --> 00:04:36,639
I'll be right back.

71
00:04:50,000 --> 00:04:51,000
Roasted sweet potatoes!

72
00:04:51,480 --> 00:04:53,600
Roasted sweet potatoes, two yuan a jin!

73
00:04:54,639 --> 00:04:55,639
Roasted sweet potatoes!

74
00:04:55,920 --> 00:04:57,240
Roasted sweet potatoes from Longkou!

75
00:05:10,600 --> 00:05:11,079
Dad!

76
00:05:11,839 --> 00:05:12,279
Dad!

77
00:05:12,759 --> 00:05:13,360
Open up!

78
00:05:14,959 --> 00:05:15,399
Dad!

79
00:05:17,160 --> 00:05:17,720
Open the door!

80
00:05:19,040 --> 00:05:19,480
Dad!

81
00:05:22,120 --> 00:05:22,680
Hey, bro.

82
00:05:22,800 --> 00:05:23,399
This is so embarrassing.

83
00:05:23,399 --> 00:05:24,600
Everyone can hear him this early.

84
00:05:24,600 --> 00:05:25,199
Open up!

85
00:05:25,519 --> 00:05:26,240
I'll throw him out.

86
00:05:27,079 --> 00:05:27,439
Right, do that.

87
00:05:27,720 --> 00:05:28,480
Don't let him keep shouting at the door.

88
00:05:28,759 --> 00:05:29,240
He's just disgracing himself!

89
00:05:29,759 --> 00:05:30,839
Dad, open the door!

90
00:05:31,759 --> 00:05:32,199
Dad!

91
00:05:32,519 --> 00:05:33,360
Stop knocking! Stop knocking!

92
00:05:35,199 --> 00:05:35,959
I need to talk to Dad!

93
00:05:35,959 --> 00:05:36,800
What could you possibly need?

94
00:05:36,800 --> 00:05:37,480
It's urgent!

95
00:05:37,480 --> 00:05:38,759
Wasn't your "urgent business" already settled?

96
00:05:39,000 --> 00:05:40,120
It's my business, and you can't handle it!

97
00:05:40,600 --> 00:05:41,560
Hold on! Don't barge in!

98
00:05:41,879 --> 00:05:42,480
Get out of my way!

99
00:05:42,480 --> 00:05:43,879
Dad already said, about that Port Authority matter...

100
00:05:44,639 --> 00:05:45,759
Dad told you to leave!

101
00:05:46,079 --> 00:05:47,120
Why... Why didn't you stop him?

102
00:05:47,120 --> 00:05:47,759
Dad! Dad!

103
00:05:48,279 --> 00:05:48,600
Dad!

104
00:05:51,000 --> 00:05:51,480
Where's Dad?

105
00:05:56,199 --> 00:05:56,720
Where is he?

106
00:05:58,000 --> 00:05:58,600
Dad! Dad!

107
00:06:02,720 --> 00:06:03,040
Look,

108
00:06:03,279 --> 00:06:04,600
even if I told you where Dad went,

109
00:06:04,839 --> 00:06:05,720
do you think he'd see you?

110
00:06:05,839 --> 00:06:07,319
Isn't it obvious he refuses to see you?

111
00:06:07,759 --> 00:06:09,199
Don't you know what you did wrong?

112
00:06:09,360 --> 00:06:10,079
Figure it out before you come back!

113
00:06:10,079 --> 00:06:11,439
Sai Xiuliang, I told you!

114
00:06:11,439 --> 00:06:12,480
If you had pushed to split the money earlier,

115
00:06:12,480 --> 00:06:13,240
if you'd just done it sooner,

116
00:06:13,240 --> 00:06:14,839
would Wen Jiayin have found an opening?

117
00:06:15,639 --> 00:06:16,759
Now we can't divide the money,

118
00:06:16,759 --> 00:06:17,839
and you've thrown the house into chaos!

119
00:06:17,839 --> 00:06:18,680
What good did that do you?

120
00:06:18,959 --> 00:06:19,519
Who are you talking to?

121
00:06:19,720 --> 00:06:20,639
Why drag your sister-in-law into this?

122
00:06:20,800 --> 00:06:21,959
Is this about the money?

123
00:06:22,040 --> 00:06:23,199
We're talking about his resignation now!

124
00:06:23,439 --> 00:06:24,199
Second Brother, let me tell you this:

125
00:06:24,639 --> 00:06:25,319
Dad made it crystal clear.

126
00:06:25,839 --> 00:06:26,920
If you don't go back to the Port Authority,

127
00:06:27,199 --> 00:06:27,600
don't you ever...

128
00:06:27,759 --> 00:06:28,439
set foot in this house again!

129
00:06:28,439 --> 00:06:29,040
Did you get that?

130
00:06:29,319 --> 00:06:30,519
Just looking at you pisses me off!

131
00:06:30,519 --> 00:06:30,839
Let me tell you,

132
00:06:30,839 --> 00:06:31,639
you went off and opened a law firm,

133
00:06:31,639 --> 00:06:32,680
and you've turned our lives upside down!

134
00:06:32,879 --> 00:06:33,399
Get out of here right now!

135
00:06:34,759 --> 00:06:35,879
How can you talk to your brother like that?

136
00:06:36,519 --> 00:06:36,839
Look...

137
00:06:37,360 --> 00:06:37,720
Second Brother,

138
00:06:38,199 --> 00:06:39,360
have you figured things out yet?

139
00:06:40,879 --> 00:06:41,920
Come back once you've thought it through.

140
00:06:43,240 --> 00:06:43,839
Otherwise, Dad...

141
00:06:44,040 --> 00:06:45,079
Dad really won't see you.

142
00:06:54,920 --> 00:06:55,639
Coming!

143
00:06:57,439 --> 00:06:59,199
Hi, who are you looking for?

144
00:07:00,279 --> 00:07:01,879
You must be Xiao Guo's fiancée.

145
00:07:02,279 --> 00:07:03,360
You're really pretty.

146
00:07:04,639 --> 00:07:05,439
Babe!

147
00:07:05,959 --> 00:07:07,360
Babe, someone's here to see you!

148
00:07:08,040 --> 00:07:09,279
If you don't give us an explanation today,

149
00:07:09,439 --> 00:07:11,160
you're not putting up this wall!

150
00:07:13,560 --> 00:07:14,360
What's going on?

151
00:07:14,639 --> 00:07:14,920
Bro!

152
00:07:14,920 --> 00:07:15,199
Jiao!

153
00:07:15,199 --> 00:07:16,160
All you workers, listen up!

154
00:07:16,160 --> 00:07:16,879
Who the hell do you think you are?

155
00:07:16,879 --> 00:07:18,199
What's with this huge mob? What's going on?

156
00:07:18,639 --> 00:07:20,319
We're building a wall for our site,

157
00:07:20,639 --> 00:07:21,720
but when the villagers heard about it,

158
00:07:21,720 --> 00:07:23,160
they all swarmed over.

159
00:07:23,160 --> 00:07:24,800
They say the demo funds haven't cleared,

160
00:07:25,040 --> 00:07:26,199
so they won't let us build!

161
00:07:26,480 --> 00:07:28,079
Brother Xiuming, think of something!

162
00:07:28,279 --> 00:07:29,959
Jiao, wait here for me.

163
00:07:32,240 --> 00:07:32,639
Biaozi!

164
00:07:34,800 --> 00:07:36,360
Tell our men to start building.

165
00:07:36,639 --> 00:07:37,199
Are you sure?

166
00:07:37,360 --> 00:07:38,279
It'll be fine. Listen to me.

167
00:07:38,399 --> 00:07:38,720
Get to work!

168
00:07:39,000 --> 00:07:39,519
Boys!

169
00:07:40,079 --> 00:07:41,319
Grab your tools and build the wall!

170
00:07:41,879 --> 00:07:42,639
Come on, get to work!

171
00:07:43,720 --> 00:07:44,879
Build it! Move it, move it!

172
00:07:45,319 --> 00:07:47,000
Ladies, please step aside!

173
00:07:48,560 --> 00:07:49,360
He's the leader!

174
00:07:49,360 --> 00:07:49,839
What are you doing?!

175
00:07:50,360 --> 00:07:51,000
Get him!

176
00:07:57,600 --> 00:07:58,000
Watch out!

177
00:07:59,879 --> 00:08:00,600
Put that down.

178
00:08:02,319 --> 00:08:02,680
Get down.

179
00:08:08,839 --> 00:08:09,120
Bro.

180
00:08:09,560 --> 00:08:10,279
Are you okay?

181
00:08:10,360 --> 00:08:11,040
Are you alright?

182
00:08:11,040 --> 00:08:11,639
I'm fine.

183
00:08:11,879 --> 00:08:13,240
That punk really didn't hold back.

184
00:08:13,639 --> 00:08:14,360
That blow really did a number on me.

185
00:08:14,639 --> 00:08:15,800
Try moving it. Can you move?

186
00:08:17,040 --> 00:08:17,519
No, no.

187
00:08:18,079 --> 00:08:18,959
Ow, ow, ow!

188
00:08:19,199 --> 00:08:20,480
Then come to the clinic with me in a bit.

189
00:08:20,720 --> 00:08:21,040
Okay.

190
00:08:21,959 --> 00:08:22,839
This wedding dress...

191
00:08:23,319 --> 00:08:25,040
I sewed it stitch by stitch.

192
00:08:25,839 --> 00:08:26,879
It's completely handmade.

193
00:08:27,519 --> 00:08:29,000
It might not be from Italy,

194
00:08:29,519 --> 00:08:30,800
but it's from Qingyangli.

195
00:08:31,519 --> 00:08:33,639
Sis, you really went all out.

196
00:08:33,919 --> 00:08:35,360
How did you know my measurements?

197
00:08:35,759 --> 00:08:37,279
Your Guo gave them to me.

198
00:08:37,360 --> 00:08:38,840
You think I just guessed?

199
00:08:39,279 --> 00:08:39,720
Sis,

200
00:08:39,919 --> 00:08:40,840
last time I went to the shop,

201
00:08:40,840 --> 00:08:41,759
I saw this style,

202
00:08:42,200 --> 00:08:43,720
and it was over 10,000 yuan.

203
00:08:43,720 --> 00:08:44,559
Over 10,000?

204
00:08:45,840 --> 00:08:47,639
Isn't that a total rip-off?

205
00:08:48,039 --> 00:08:48,519
Sis,

206
00:08:48,679 --> 00:08:49,720
just out of curiosity...

207
00:08:49,960 --> 00:08:51,960
How much did this dress cost you to make?

208
00:08:52,240 --> 00:08:54,000
Normally, that's a trade secret,

209
00:08:55,000 --> 00:08:55,840
but between us,

210
00:08:55,840 --> 00:08:56,600
I can tell you.

211
00:08:57,080 --> 00:08:58,720
Materials plus labor,

212
00:08:58,720 --> 00:08:59,159
at most,

213
00:08:59,759 --> 00:09:00,360
800 yuan.

214
00:09:00,639 --> 00:09:01,440
800?

215
00:09:01,440 --> 00:09:03,000
Yeah, I sewed it myself, after all.

216
00:09:03,120 --> 00:09:03,559
That's...

217
00:09:04,039 --> 00:09:05,720
That's an insane price difference!

218
00:09:05,720 --> 00:09:06,159
Tell me about it!

219
00:09:06,480 --> 00:09:07,440
If you ask me, Sis,

220
00:09:07,879 --> 00:09:09,279
don't let this skill go to waste.

221
00:09:09,440 --> 00:09:10,120
Let's open a shop!

222
00:09:11,919 --> 00:09:12,519
Do you like it?

223
00:09:13,519 --> 00:09:14,440
As long as you like it.

224
00:09:14,879 --> 00:09:15,480
Guo,

225
00:09:16,039 --> 00:09:17,039
don't feel burdened, okay?

226
00:09:17,519 --> 00:09:18,480
The money for this wedding dress,

227
00:09:18,480 --> 00:09:20,440
I earned it sewing dresses on the side.

228
00:09:20,440 --> 00:09:21,960
It's got nothing to do with the site.

229
00:09:22,120 --> 00:09:23,240
Take it without worry.

230
00:09:23,559 --> 00:09:25,039
Consider it my cash gift.

231
00:09:25,720 --> 00:09:27,120
Wishing you a long, happy marriage,

232
00:09:27,960 --> 00:09:28,679
and a lovely baby soon.

233
00:09:28,679 --> 00:09:29,519
Thanks, Sis.

234
00:09:29,519 --> 00:09:30,559
I still have to go back and cook.

235
00:09:30,559 --> 00:09:31,360
I'll get going now.

236
00:09:31,399 --> 00:09:32,240
Take care, Sis.

237
00:09:32,360 --> 00:09:32,840
It's so gorgeous.

238
00:09:32,840 --> 00:09:33,519
Sis,

239
00:09:33,639 --> 00:09:35,320
remember to come to the wedding!

240
00:09:35,600 --> 00:09:37,000
I'll send you an invitation!

241
00:09:37,120 --> 00:09:37,600
Honey!

242
00:09:42,759 --> 00:09:44,120
No need to see me out, really.

243
00:09:44,360 --> 00:09:44,679
Sis!

244
00:09:49,720 --> 00:09:50,240
Hurry up,

245
00:09:50,720 --> 00:09:51,639
go check on the construction site!

246
00:09:53,679 --> 00:09:54,279
Easy, take it easy.

247
00:09:56,080 --> 00:09:56,519
Look at this.

248
00:09:58,480 --> 00:09:58,840
Right here.

249
00:10:02,679 --> 00:10:03,440
Let me disinfect it first.

250
00:10:05,279 --> 00:10:05,559
Ow.

251
00:10:06,679 --> 00:10:07,159
Does it hurt?

252
00:10:07,679 --> 00:10:08,480
No, it doesn't hurt.

253
00:10:08,600 --> 00:10:10,080
It's just cold. Cold.

254
00:10:10,559 --> 00:10:11,240
Bear with it for a second.

255
00:10:13,120 --> 00:10:14,960
Thanks to you today, Brother Xiuming.

256
00:10:18,519 --> 00:10:19,960
Why are you being so polite with me?

257
00:10:20,480 --> 00:10:21,440
How many years has it been for us?

258
00:10:22,200 --> 00:10:22,559
It's nothing.

259
00:10:22,879 --> 00:10:24,440
You're really amazing, Brother Xiuming.

260
00:10:25,039 --> 00:10:26,240
Whenever something happened growing up,

261
00:10:26,240 --> 00:10:27,559
you were always the first to step up.

262
00:10:28,480 --> 00:10:28,799
Me?

263
00:10:29,120 --> 00:10:30,039
What's so amazing about me?

264
00:10:30,279 --> 00:10:30,919
I just...

265
00:10:31,120 --> 00:10:32,200
got beaten up by someone.

266
00:10:32,320 --> 00:10:33,200
What's so great about that?

267
00:10:33,320 --> 00:10:34,879
That's only because you didn't hit back.

268
00:10:34,879 --> 00:10:35,879
Not like you couldn't beat him.

269
00:10:36,840 --> 00:10:38,440
Everyone at the site says

270
00:10:38,559 --> 00:10:40,240
that you're a really good man.

271
00:10:40,759 --> 00:10:41,720
You never look for trouble,

272
00:10:41,720 --> 00:10:42,799
but you never run from it either.

273
00:10:43,759 --> 00:10:45,879
If my family's crew ever closes down,

274
00:10:46,120 --> 00:10:47,240
probably more than half the workers

275
00:10:47,240 --> 00:10:48,200
would go join you instead.

276
00:10:55,159 --> 00:10:55,720
Lao Zhao,

277
00:10:56,440 --> 00:10:57,759
mix that batch up for me first,

278
00:10:57,759 --> 00:10:58,600
and set it aside.

279
00:10:59,240 --> 00:10:59,639
All right, all right.

280
00:10:59,639 --> 00:11:00,759
Wait for my word later.

281
00:11:01,080 --> 00:11:01,919
Just set it aside.

282
00:11:01,919 --> 00:11:02,639
Leave it alone!

283
00:11:03,039 --> 00:11:03,879
Sure thing, Brother Qingyou.

284
00:11:06,879 --> 00:11:08,799
Put yours over on that side too.

285
00:11:14,600 --> 00:11:15,120
Sister-in-law.

286
00:11:16,480 --> 00:11:17,919
What... What are you doing here?

287
00:11:18,120 --> 00:11:18,799
Is something wrong?

288
00:11:23,879 --> 00:11:24,240
Here.

289
00:11:24,679 --> 00:11:25,120
Take this.

290
00:11:25,559 --> 00:11:26,759
What are you doing, Sister-in-law?

291
00:11:27,159 --> 00:11:27,600
Qingyou.

292
00:11:27,840 --> 00:11:29,720
I'm here to apologize for your Brother Xiuming.

293
00:11:30,720 --> 00:11:31,159
There's really no need.

294
00:11:31,159 --> 00:11:31,919
That day...

295
00:11:32,000 --> 00:11:33,200
He let a little authority go to his head.

296
00:11:33,240 --> 00:11:34,320
With your Uncle Duoxi away,

297
00:11:34,879 --> 00:11:36,440
he forgot his place.

298
00:11:36,960 --> 00:11:37,879
He said those terrible things.

299
00:11:37,879 --> 00:11:38,879
Please don't take it to heart.

300
00:11:39,240 --> 00:11:40,039
You have to take this.

301
00:11:40,399 --> 00:11:41,519
I'm just a hired hand.

302
00:11:41,519 --> 00:11:42,559
I... I can't accept this.

303
00:11:42,559 --> 00:11:44,120
You're still mad, aren't you?

304
00:11:44,120 --> 00:11:45,840
Who am I to be mad?

305
00:11:46,360 --> 00:11:47,480
Sister-in-law, if you're done,

306
00:11:47,480 --> 00:11:48,039
why don't you head back?

307
00:11:48,039 --> 00:11:48,519
Qingyou.

308
00:11:49,080 --> 00:11:49,720
Answer me honestly.

309
00:11:50,480 --> 00:11:51,120
This batch of sand...

310
00:11:51,759 --> 00:11:52,960
Did it come in last night?

311
00:11:54,759 --> 00:11:55,360
How do you know?

312
00:11:55,679 --> 00:11:56,039
I...

313
00:11:56,440 --> 00:11:57,080
I don't know anything about it.

314
00:11:59,159 --> 00:11:59,639
Last night,

315
00:11:59,639 --> 00:12:00,559
weren't you on shift?

316
00:12:00,840 --> 00:12:01,720
How could you not know?

317
00:12:03,120 --> 00:12:03,919
I just don't know!

318
00:12:05,919 --> 00:12:06,480
This batch of sand,

319
00:12:06,879 --> 00:12:08,159
did it arrive last night?

320
00:12:09,399 --> 00:12:10,159
You don't know?

321
00:12:10,320 --> 00:12:11,000
I don't!

322
00:12:11,240 --> 00:12:11,840
I really don't!

323
00:12:12,639 --> 00:12:14,360
Wait, what are you doing, Sister-in-law?

324
00:12:17,480 --> 00:12:18,080
Tell them to stop.

325
00:12:18,519 --> 00:12:19,279
Why should they stop?

326
00:12:19,879 --> 00:12:20,799
They can't just stop because you say so!

327
00:12:20,799 --> 00:12:22,279
Do you know how much time that'll waste?

328
00:12:22,440 --> 00:12:23,480
All of you in the Sai family,

329
00:12:23,480 --> 00:12:24,080
you just love messing with me, don't you?

330
00:12:24,080 --> 00:12:25,480
Yang Qingyou, you're pushing your luck!

331
00:12:26,399 --> 00:12:27,240
Did the old supervisor

332
00:12:27,240 --> 00:12:28,360
haul this in last night?

333
00:12:28,679 --> 00:12:29,240
What was mixed in?

334
00:12:29,440 --> 00:12:30,679
Do you want me to say it out loud

335
00:12:30,679 --> 00:12:31,559
in front of everyone?

336
00:12:32,320 --> 00:12:33,320
What are you talking about?

337
00:12:33,320 --> 00:12:34,240
I... I don't know what you mean.

338
00:12:34,240 --> 00:12:35,879
You teamed up with a fired supervisor

339
00:12:35,879 --> 00:12:36,679
to pull this scheme,

340
00:12:36,919 --> 00:12:39,200
ruining our own site with sea sand!

341
00:12:39,639 --> 00:12:40,879
That's a crime!

342
00:12:41,000 --> 00:12:41,879
If this blows up,

343
00:12:41,919 --> 00:12:42,519
do you think you can handle it?

344
00:12:42,519 --> 00:12:43,000
I didn't!

345
00:12:43,279 --> 00:12:43,879
I really didn't!

346
00:12:43,919 --> 00:12:44,279
Fine.

347
00:12:45,519 --> 00:12:46,279
Let's call the police.

348
00:12:46,720 --> 00:12:47,480
Let the cops come,

349
00:12:48,000 --> 00:12:48,799
bring their testing gear,

350
00:12:49,080 --> 00:12:49,840
and test it on the spot!

351
00:12:50,399 --> 00:12:51,600
Let's see if one word from me

352
00:12:51,600 --> 00:12:52,919
sends you straight to prison!

353
00:12:57,120 --> 00:12:57,559
Stop!

354
00:12:58,200 --> 00:12:58,600
Stop!

355
00:12:59,480 --> 00:12:59,879
Stop!

356
00:13:00,720 --> 00:13:01,639
Everyone, stop right now!

357
00:13:02,159 --> 00:13:03,120
Stop, shut it down!

358
00:13:03,320 --> 00:13:04,240
Shovel all this out!

359
00:13:04,440 --> 00:13:05,759
There's sea sand in here! Scrap it!

360
00:13:05,879 --> 00:13:06,279
Loader!

361
00:13:06,279 --> 00:13:06,759
It's all junk!

362
00:13:06,759 --> 00:13:07,240
This sand...

363
00:13:07,399 --> 00:13:08,960
Get all this sand hauled out of here!

364
00:13:09,480 --> 00:13:10,360
Shovel it all into the loader!

365
00:13:10,360 --> 00:13:11,320
Throw it all out!

366
00:13:11,320 --> 00:13:11,879
Did you hear me?

367
00:13:11,919 --> 00:13:12,559
Okay, got it!

368
00:13:12,759 --> 00:13:13,919
Just dump it in a minute

369
00:13:13,919 --> 00:13:14,960
in that empty lot by the village entrance.

370
00:13:14,960 --> 00:13:15,639
That'll do it.

371
00:13:15,960 --> 00:13:16,759
Hurry it up!

372
00:13:16,759 --> 00:13:18,559
Dump it by the village entrance.

373
00:13:18,679 --> 00:13:19,039
Okay.

374
00:13:19,039 --> 00:13:19,960
Right on that empty lot.

375
00:13:19,960 --> 00:13:20,720
That'll be fine.

376
00:13:21,039 --> 00:13:21,519
Haul it out!

377
00:13:21,720 --> 00:13:22,759
Careful! Out of the way!

378
00:13:23,720 --> 00:13:24,440
Move, move!

379
00:13:25,240 --> 00:13:25,679
Watch out!

380
00:13:25,679 --> 00:13:26,200
Make way! Move aside!

381
00:13:26,399 --> 00:13:27,840
Watch out! Pull forward a bit!

382
00:13:28,000 --> 00:13:29,000
Can you guys move any faster?

383
00:13:35,440 --> 00:13:36,000
In the future,

384
00:13:36,159 --> 00:13:37,039
we at Tengyue Group

385
00:13:37,200 --> 00:13:38,600
have the capability and confidence,

386
00:13:38,840 --> 00:13:41,000
with our leaders' support and guidance,

387
00:13:41,440 --> 00:13:42,120
to transform this place

388
00:13:42,519 --> 00:13:45,399
into a world-class benchmark.

389
00:13:48,840 --> 00:13:49,320
Excuse me.

390
00:13:49,519 --> 00:13:50,200
Over here is Pier 1.

391
00:13:50,200 --> 00:13:50,559
President Shi.

392
00:13:51,559 --> 00:13:52,360
Leaders, excuse me for a moment.

393
00:13:53,559 --> 00:13:54,120
What is it?

394
00:13:54,240 --> 00:13:54,919
What's wrong? What happened?

395
00:13:57,320 --> 00:13:58,080
Something happened at the site.

396
00:14:00,639 --> 00:14:01,440
What bad luck.

397
00:14:01,840 --> 00:14:02,879
Coming all the way out here,

398
00:14:02,879 --> 00:14:03,559
and we didn't find a thing.

399
00:14:04,120 --> 00:14:05,639
Right? We've been in construction

400
00:14:05,639 --> 00:14:06,600
for so many years.

401
00:14:07,000 --> 00:14:09,039
Mixing sea sand into the materials...

402
00:14:09,039 --> 00:14:10,559
We'd never do such a thing.

403
00:14:10,639 --> 00:14:11,360
On that tip-off call,

404
00:14:11,360 --> 00:14:12,639
they made it sound so convincing.

405
00:14:12,919 --> 00:14:14,559
Midnight deliveries, using shoddy goods.

406
00:14:14,879 --> 00:14:15,279
What's the deal?

407
00:14:15,480 --> 00:14:16,480
They're just using us as pawns!

408
00:14:17,000 --> 00:14:17,840
Whoever reported us,

409
00:14:17,840 --> 00:14:19,440
we must've pissed someone off.

410
00:14:19,440 --> 00:14:19,960
All right, all right.

411
00:14:21,759 --> 00:14:22,120
Watch your step.

412
00:14:24,000 --> 00:14:25,559
Sorry to make you come out for nothing.

413
00:14:25,559 --> 00:14:26,120
Take care, now.

414
00:14:31,519 --> 00:14:32,159
Uncle's here.

415
00:14:36,360 --> 00:14:37,799
Dad, what brought you here?

416
00:14:38,120 --> 00:14:39,360
Old Wei called me,

417
00:14:39,440 --> 00:14:40,720
saying someone reported our site.

418
00:14:40,799 --> 00:14:41,559
Even the inspection team showed up.

419
00:14:41,559 --> 00:14:42,440
What's going on?

420
00:14:42,840 --> 00:14:43,200
Well...

421
00:14:43,519 --> 00:14:45,200
They got an anonymous tip this morning,

422
00:14:45,200 --> 00:14:46,600
saying our materials were substandard.

423
00:14:46,799 --> 00:14:48,679
They checked the new batch of materials,

424
00:14:48,879 --> 00:14:50,000
and the earlier batches too.

425
00:14:50,000 --> 00:14:50,559
Nothing was wrong.

426
00:14:50,559 --> 00:14:51,399
So they just left.

427
00:14:51,840 --> 00:14:52,240
That's not right.

428
00:14:52,879 --> 00:14:54,120
He mentioned something about sea sand.

429
00:14:55,120 --> 00:14:55,919
Who was on duty last night?

430
00:14:58,240 --> 00:14:59,240
Who was on duty last night?

431
00:15:00,600 --> 00:15:01,320
I was on duty.

432
00:15:01,320 --> 00:15:02,000
You tell me what happened.

433
00:15:02,799 --> 00:15:03,200
Dad,

434
00:15:03,840 --> 00:15:05,720
I just figured it out.

435
00:15:05,960 --> 00:15:07,399
A new worker at our site

436
00:15:08,039 --> 00:15:10,360
colluded with the old supervisor

437
00:15:10,799 --> 00:15:11,840
to get revenge on us.

438
00:15:12,159 --> 00:15:12,639
Where's that worker?

439
00:15:12,639 --> 00:15:13,200
Bring him here.

440
00:15:13,240 --> 00:15:13,679
I'll question him.

441
00:15:13,919 --> 00:15:14,960
In a fit of anger,

442
00:15:14,960 --> 00:15:15,919
I fired him.

443
00:15:17,000 --> 00:15:17,840
You just found out,

444
00:15:17,840 --> 00:15:18,399
and you fired him right away?

445
00:15:18,679 --> 00:15:19,639
Why didn't you ask me first?

446
00:15:19,960 --> 00:15:21,200
A traitorous scoundrel like that,

447
00:15:21,200 --> 00:15:22,399
why keep him around?

448
00:15:23,120 --> 00:15:24,159
Besides, Dad,

449
00:15:24,559 --> 00:15:25,120
let's not make a big deal of this.

450
00:15:25,559 --> 00:15:26,440
If word gets out,

451
00:15:26,879 --> 00:15:28,600
people will say we can't manage our site.

452
00:15:29,039 --> 00:15:29,360
Right?

453
00:15:30,240 --> 00:15:30,559
Dad,

454
00:15:31,039 --> 00:15:32,559
it's all thanks to Qingyou today.

455
00:15:33,240 --> 00:15:34,440
He acted fast,

456
00:15:34,840 --> 00:15:36,720
so before they arrived,

457
00:15:36,720 --> 00:15:38,159
he got all that sand cleared away.

458
00:15:38,399 --> 00:15:39,080
Not a trace left.

459
00:15:39,320 --> 00:15:39,919
Completely clean.

460
00:15:42,159 --> 00:15:43,399
It's hard to guard against a thief within.

461
00:15:45,799 --> 00:15:46,440
Where's the eldest?

462
00:15:46,720 --> 00:15:48,399
Isn't something going on at the Ma site?

463
00:15:48,399 --> 00:15:49,399
He went over to help.

464
00:15:49,759 --> 00:15:50,039
All right.

465
00:15:50,159 --> 00:15:51,200
Come on, let's go have a look.

466
00:16:02,399 --> 00:16:02,720
Dad,

467
00:16:03,279 --> 00:16:04,799
staying by your side these past two days...

468
00:16:05,279 --> 00:16:06,679
...keeps bringing back childhood memories.

469
00:16:07,240 --> 00:16:08,080
Back then,

470
00:16:09,399 --> 00:16:10,080
whenever I fell sick,

471
00:16:12,159 --> 00:16:13,759
you and Mom watched over me just like this.

472
00:16:15,240 --> 00:16:15,799
Later on,

473
00:16:16,720 --> 00:16:17,240
Mom passed away,

474
00:16:17,919 --> 00:16:19,000
leaving you all by yourself.

475
00:16:20,720 --> 00:16:21,639
Life got even tougher,

476
00:16:24,360 --> 00:16:25,120
and you were so lonely.

477
00:16:27,679 --> 00:16:28,440
Now that you're sick,

478
00:16:30,679 --> 00:16:31,639
I've completely realized it.

479
00:16:32,360 --> 00:16:33,360
Money and all that...

480
00:16:34,120 --> 00:16:35,720
compared to your health,

481
00:16:36,120 --> 00:16:36,960
it's not worth a single cent.

482
00:16:38,960 --> 00:16:39,519
Laiqi.

483
00:16:40,600 --> 00:16:40,879
Dad?

484
00:16:41,600 --> 00:16:42,720
Do you really mean that?

485
00:16:42,960 --> 00:16:44,120
Of course I do!

486
00:16:44,960 --> 00:16:45,440
I mean,

487
00:16:45,679 --> 00:16:46,799
if you were gone,

488
00:16:47,759 --> 00:16:49,080
what would I have left to hold onto?

489
00:16:51,200 --> 00:16:51,879
I've made up my mind.

490
00:16:53,000 --> 00:16:53,960
As soon as you're discharged,

491
00:16:54,519 --> 00:16:55,759
I'm bringing you home to live with us.

492
00:16:55,919 --> 00:16:57,039
I'll make more time

493
00:16:57,600 --> 00:16:58,399
just to be there with you.

494
00:16:59,200 --> 00:16:59,879
Our family,

495
00:17:00,360 --> 00:17:02,279
living in peace and harmony...

496
00:17:02,600 --> 00:17:04,319
Isn't that better than anything, Dad?

497
00:17:08,200 --> 00:17:08,599
Then...

498
00:17:09,759 --> 00:17:11,160
what about Laibu and Laijiao?

499
00:17:25,000 --> 00:17:25,319
Dad,

500
00:17:26,240 --> 00:17:27,039
have an apple.

501
00:17:32,079 --> 00:17:32,799
As for Laibu,

502
00:17:33,720 --> 00:17:34,799
he can't hold on to money.

503
00:17:35,680 --> 00:17:36,559
If you don't give him anything,

504
00:17:37,279 --> 00:17:38,240
he definitely won't stand for it.

505
00:17:39,640 --> 00:17:40,200
If you ask me,

506
00:17:40,599 --> 00:17:42,839
just give him 1.5 million outright,

507
00:17:43,160 --> 00:17:44,319
let him buy an apartment himself,

508
00:17:44,920 --> 00:17:45,559
and use what's left

509
00:17:45,720 --> 00:17:47,000
as startup capital for a business.

510
00:17:47,400 --> 00:17:48,200
Whether he succeeds or fails,

511
00:17:48,400 --> 00:17:49,799
that's up to his own luck.

512
00:17:51,160 --> 00:17:52,279
At least that way, our family

513
00:17:52,799 --> 00:17:53,519
will have done our duty by him.

514
00:17:56,440 --> 00:17:57,640
And as for Laijiao,

515
00:17:58,319 --> 00:17:59,519
she's bound to remarry eventually.

516
00:18:00,720 --> 00:18:02,640
You always look out for your youngest,

517
00:18:03,240 --> 00:18:05,160
but you can't keep her around forever.

518
00:18:05,880 --> 00:18:07,039
Or she really will end up an old maid.

519
00:18:08,160 --> 00:18:08,960
As for the rest of the money,

520
00:18:09,440 --> 00:18:10,359
I don't want a single cent.

521
00:18:10,960 --> 00:18:12,000
Keep it all for your retirement.

522
00:18:14,599 --> 00:18:15,319
All right.

523
00:18:16,960 --> 00:18:17,839
Everything you've said,

524
00:18:19,000 --> 00:18:20,319
I've taken it to heart.

525
00:18:21,240 --> 00:18:22,119
Have an apple yourself.

526
00:18:24,160 --> 00:18:25,000
No, thanks.

527
00:18:25,880 --> 00:18:27,559
I want to take a nap.

528
00:18:35,160 --> 00:18:35,680
Auntie,

529
00:18:36,240 --> 00:18:37,519
Ma Laiqi went to see my dad today,

530
00:18:37,880 --> 00:18:39,359
crying his eyes out,

531
00:18:39,960 --> 00:18:40,920
just trying to get a bigger cut,

532
00:18:41,400 --> 00:18:42,279
maybe even leave me with nothing.

533
00:18:43,359 --> 00:18:44,279
How do you know that?

534
00:18:45,079 --> 00:18:46,160
I've got people at the hospital.

535
00:18:47,839 --> 00:18:48,240
Auntie,

536
00:18:48,559 --> 00:18:49,359
my dad only trusts you.

537
00:18:50,720 --> 00:18:51,759
He even handed the account books to you.

538
00:18:52,519 --> 00:18:54,079
You practically run the family now,

539
00:18:54,559 --> 00:18:55,759
like a second mother to me.

540
00:18:57,200 --> 00:18:58,240
Please help me out.

541
00:18:58,640 --> 00:18:59,440
You've got to find a way

542
00:18:59,720 --> 00:19:00,839
to get me a bigger share.

543
00:19:01,880 --> 00:19:02,799
And what's in it for me?

544
00:19:04,000 --> 00:19:05,200
If I get you an extra 500,000,

545
00:19:05,200 --> 00:19:05,920
what do I get?

546
00:19:06,720 --> 00:19:07,000
Wait,

547
00:19:07,480 --> 00:19:08,319
what do you want?

548
00:19:08,759 --> 00:19:09,720
Find me a good apartment.

549
00:19:10,720 --> 00:19:11,160
No problem.

550
00:19:12,000 --> 00:19:12,680
Leave it to me.

551
00:19:16,079 --> 00:19:17,039
Why hasn't that guy arrived yet?

552
00:19:17,599 --> 00:19:18,400
My third brother, you mean?

553
00:19:19,000 --> 00:19:19,920
He should be here soon.

554
00:19:22,079 --> 00:19:22,519
Tell me,

555
00:19:23,440 --> 00:19:24,559
between you and Old Third Sai,

556
00:19:24,720 --> 00:19:25,599
how close are you really?

557
00:19:25,960 --> 00:19:27,039
He's like an older brother to me.

558
00:19:27,680 --> 00:19:28,680
We grew up together.

559
00:19:29,160 --> 00:19:30,720
Though I'm actually a lot older than him,

560
00:19:30,880 --> 00:19:32,559
we go by street hierarchy.

561
00:19:33,160 --> 00:19:35,359
He took me to make money selling houses.

562
00:19:35,799 --> 00:19:36,799
What kind of guy is he really?

563
00:19:37,200 --> 00:19:38,559
He's a real shrewd operator.

564
00:19:43,279 --> 00:19:44,319
I'll go get dinner ready, Dad.

565
00:19:44,960 --> 00:19:45,480
Zhenzhu's mom,

566
00:19:47,599 --> 00:19:47,880
sit down.

567
00:19:48,200 --> 00:19:48,680
Sit for a bit.

568
00:19:56,440 --> 00:19:57,079
Just tell me

569
00:19:59,160 --> 00:20:00,440
the honest truth.

570
00:20:02,480 --> 00:20:03,799
About what happened today,

571
00:20:06,400 --> 00:20:08,400
did Yang Qingyou have a hand in it?

572
00:20:14,720 --> 00:20:15,839
Dad, you asked me to speak up.

573
00:20:17,680 --> 00:20:18,519
Truth is,

574
00:20:20,319 --> 00:20:21,200
it's understandable.

575
00:20:21,799 --> 00:20:23,599
Xiuming audited Qingyou's books,

576
00:20:23,759 --> 00:20:25,200
figured out every single detail,

577
00:20:25,279 --> 00:20:26,240
and called him out right then and there,

578
00:20:26,400 --> 00:20:28,000
totally humiliating Qingyou.

579
00:20:28,319 --> 00:20:29,759
Wasn't that a slap in the face?

580
00:20:30,079 --> 00:20:31,079
Who keeps one set of books for show

581
00:20:31,079 --> 00:20:32,079
and another behind people's backs?

582
00:20:40,960 --> 00:20:41,319
Well,

583
00:20:42,240 --> 00:20:43,000
what else?

584
00:20:43,519 --> 00:20:45,720
If we only trust Yang Qingyou,

585
00:20:46,759 --> 00:20:47,319
then...

586
00:20:47,920 --> 00:20:48,319
then whose

587
00:20:48,960 --> 00:20:50,640
are these accounts? Yang's,

588
00:20:51,079 --> 00:20:51,920
or Sai's?

589
00:20:52,480 --> 00:20:52,880
Dad,

590
00:20:54,039 --> 00:20:55,480
that's not what I meant.

591
00:20:55,799 --> 00:20:57,039
I just feel like

592
00:20:57,359 --> 00:20:59,319
everyone gets hot-headed sometimes.

593
00:21:00,279 --> 00:21:01,039
Take me, for instance.

594
00:21:01,759 --> 00:21:02,839
I lose my head all the time.

595
00:21:05,920 --> 00:21:07,160
Dad, I've actually always wanted

596
00:21:07,160 --> 00:21:08,519
to apologize to you.

597
00:21:09,559 --> 00:21:10,559
What happened with Xiuliang...

598
00:21:11,200 --> 00:21:12,799
I really shouldn't have blabbed.

599
00:21:13,720 --> 00:21:14,440
I was just anxious.

600
00:21:15,480 --> 00:21:16,160
But I just feel,

601
00:21:16,160 --> 00:21:17,880
why didn't he tell you about this?

602
00:21:18,079 --> 00:21:18,839
For such a major thing,

603
00:21:19,279 --> 00:21:20,039
he should've at least come home

604
00:21:20,039 --> 00:21:21,000
to discuss it with you.

605
00:21:21,160 --> 00:21:22,799
How could he just quit like that?

606
00:21:27,079 --> 00:21:28,279
Is that really what you think?

607
00:21:28,440 --> 00:21:28,839
Really.

608
00:21:29,400 --> 00:21:30,119
Dad, I swear.

609
00:21:34,960 --> 00:21:35,400
Dad,

610
00:21:37,480 --> 00:21:38,839
why don't you ever believe me?

611
00:21:41,480 --> 00:21:42,079
Sorry,

612
00:21:42,279 --> 00:21:42,759
I'm late.

613
00:21:43,279 --> 00:21:43,799
Overslept.

614
00:21:43,799 --> 00:21:44,119
Bro,

615
00:21:44,519 --> 00:21:45,480
everything's ready for you.

616
00:21:45,759 --> 00:21:46,400
Still beer.

617
00:21:48,480 --> 00:21:49,440
This pretty lady...

618
00:21:49,480 --> 00:21:50,039
Call me Auntie.

619
00:21:51,359 --> 00:21:51,640
Fine.

620
00:21:52,079 --> 00:21:52,519
Auntie,

621
00:21:53,000 --> 00:21:54,960
still want to sell the crew to our family?

622
00:21:55,519 --> 00:21:55,880
Look,

623
00:21:57,000 --> 00:21:58,519
let's put our cards on the table.

624
00:21:59,119 --> 00:21:59,880
Be straight with me.

625
00:22:00,680 --> 00:22:01,640
Does your old man

626
00:22:02,240 --> 00:22:03,519
actually want this construction crew?

627
00:22:04,160 --> 00:22:05,279
Of course he wants it.

628
00:22:05,559 --> 00:22:06,480
Passing up a bargain

629
00:22:06,480 --> 00:22:07,279
would make him an idiot.

630
00:22:08,359 --> 00:22:08,880
What do you mean?

631
00:22:13,119 --> 00:22:13,559
Auntie,

632
00:22:14,200 --> 00:22:14,839
someone like you,

633
00:22:15,079 --> 00:22:16,400
you've lived in the city too long.

634
00:22:16,640 --> 00:22:18,720
You play by polite, civilized rules.

635
00:22:19,240 --> 00:22:20,160
How things work in Qingyangli...

636
00:22:20,720 --> 00:22:21,559
let me break it down for you.

637
00:22:22,039 --> 00:22:23,640
The old man is managing the crew for Old Ma,

638
00:22:24,160 --> 00:22:25,039
but that's just "helping out."

639
00:22:25,839 --> 00:22:27,640
If he wants to buy it, that costs money.

640
00:22:28,200 --> 00:22:28,960
And when it comes to money,

641
00:22:28,960 --> 00:22:30,079
pocketing it is fine,

642
00:22:30,440 --> 00:22:31,079
but shelling it out?

643
00:22:31,480 --> 00:22:31,799
No way.

644
00:22:32,200 --> 00:22:32,920
Not to mention,

645
00:22:33,200 --> 00:22:34,039
your family's construction crew

646
00:22:34,720 --> 00:22:35,240
is a total trap.

647
00:22:37,759 --> 00:22:38,359
Nephew,

648
00:22:39,519 --> 00:22:40,000
here's the thing.

649
00:22:40,319 --> 00:22:41,599
My brother-in-law's health...

650
00:22:42,119 --> 00:22:42,799
you know how it is.

651
00:22:43,599 --> 00:22:44,720
According to him,

652
00:22:45,079 --> 00:22:47,000
given the history and ties between us,

653
00:22:47,359 --> 00:22:48,640
selling to your family is definitely best.

654
00:22:49,279 --> 00:22:50,839
After all, we're basically family.

655
00:22:50,839 --> 00:22:51,200
Right?

656
00:22:56,079 --> 00:22:56,720
Let me level with you.

657
00:22:57,640 --> 00:22:58,759
My old man's vision,

658
00:22:59,279 --> 00:23:00,079
compared to Yang the Second,

659
00:23:01,039 --> 00:23:02,000
is only this much better at best.

660
00:23:03,079 --> 00:23:04,240
But I won't let you buy this for nothing.

661
00:23:04,440 --> 00:23:05,279
You just want inside information, right?

662
00:23:05,960 --> 00:23:06,880
If you trust me,

663
00:23:07,839 --> 00:23:08,440
leave your number.

664
00:23:08,960 --> 00:23:09,599
When there's any news,

665
00:23:09,599 --> 00:23:10,119
I'll let you know.

666
00:23:24,480 --> 00:23:25,720
Now that we're talking about this,

667
00:23:25,720 --> 00:23:26,279
I just want to

668
00:23:27,400 --> 00:23:28,599
ask you one more thing.

669
00:23:30,720 --> 00:23:33,160
You clearly knew that with these accounts,

670
00:23:34,240 --> 00:23:35,480
Xiuming wouldn't understand them,

671
00:23:36,079 --> 00:23:37,880
so why wouldn't you let me take a look?

672
00:23:50,160 --> 00:23:51,359
Zhenzhu's mom, you really...

673
00:23:51,480 --> 00:23:52,839
Y-You're overthinking it.

674
00:23:53,039 --> 00:23:53,359
You...

675
00:23:54,279 --> 00:23:54,599
You...

676
00:23:55,279 --> 00:23:56,559
I, I, I...

677
00:23:57,160 --> 00:23:59,039
It's not that I don't trust you.

678
00:23:59,039 --> 00:23:59,480
It's just that I...

679
00:24:00,079 --> 00:24:00,519
well...

680
00:24:03,319 --> 00:24:04,000
Just look at this:

681
00:24:04,319 --> 00:24:05,079
my oldest and second sons.

682
00:24:05,799 --> 00:24:08,079
If I give each of them a... a dollar,

683
00:24:09,559 --> 00:24:10,519
in less than two days,

684
00:24:11,880 --> 00:24:12,440
the oldest,

685
00:24:13,519 --> 00:24:14,279
his dollar is gone.

686
00:24:15,279 --> 00:24:15,960
But the second son?

687
00:24:16,759 --> 00:24:18,839
He'd bring you back a dollar fifty!

688
00:24:19,319 --> 00:24:21,599
That brain of the oldest...

689
00:24:21,599 --> 00:24:22,279
he's just...

690
00:24:23,279 --> 00:24:24,759
When he gets bullheaded,

691
00:24:25,039 --> 00:24:26,079
can you handle him?

692
00:24:26,200 --> 00:24:26,640
I can.

693
00:24:34,839 --> 00:24:35,519
You can?

694
00:24:42,200 --> 00:24:42,519
Dad,

695
00:24:45,559 --> 00:24:46,279
I'll listen to you.

696
00:24:48,440 --> 00:24:49,000
I won't pry.

697
00:24:57,240 --> 00:24:58,440
Then I just... I just...

698
00:24:58,759 --> 00:24:59,920
I just want to ask you,

699
00:25:00,640 --> 00:25:01,799
about what happened today,

700
00:25:02,799 --> 00:25:04,920
how on earth did you find out?

701
00:25:11,000 --> 00:25:12,079
Actually, over the past few years,

702
00:25:12,160 --> 00:25:12,839
outside the house,

703
00:25:12,839 --> 00:25:14,519
I've been taking on piecework,

704
00:25:14,920 --> 00:25:16,440
beading and making wedding dresses,

705
00:25:17,359 --> 00:25:18,720
just to help support the family.

706
00:25:19,319 --> 00:25:21,079
And I never neglected the household.

707
00:25:21,480 --> 00:25:22,240
Wasn't it just a coincidence?

708
00:25:22,240 --> 00:25:23,559
That young supervisor was getting married,

709
00:25:23,559 --> 00:25:25,279
so I made a gown for his bride.

710
00:25:25,279 --> 00:25:26,359
I didn't charge him.

711
00:25:27,079 --> 00:25:27,599
Maybe he was

712
00:25:28,240 --> 00:25:29,000
touched, I guess.

713
00:25:29,319 --> 00:25:30,759
Who knew it would pay off?

714
00:25:30,839 --> 00:25:31,240
So he...

715
00:25:31,880 --> 00:25:33,160
he told me all about it.

716
00:25:33,519 --> 00:25:34,319
It really goes to show,

717
00:25:35,720 --> 00:25:36,799
kindness gets rewarded.

718
00:25:37,400 --> 00:25:39,599
The bridal workshop isn't big,

719
00:25:40,039 --> 00:25:40,400
but...

720
00:25:41,279 --> 00:25:41,759
it still...

721
00:25:42,400 --> 00:25:43,440
still makes a bit of money.

722
00:25:43,680 --> 00:25:45,240
The owner said with my skill,

723
00:25:45,319 --> 00:25:46,319
just doing beading

724
00:25:46,319 --> 00:25:47,480
is kind of a waste.

725
00:25:48,240 --> 00:25:48,559
I... I was even...

726
00:25:48,559 --> 00:25:49,200
Look,

727
00:25:49,200 --> 00:25:51,519
between everything at home

728
00:25:51,720 --> 00:25:52,400
and on the construction site,

729
00:25:52,640 --> 00:25:54,440
we already have our hands full.

730
00:25:54,720 --> 00:25:55,640
As for the construction team,

731
00:25:56,160 --> 00:25:57,799
if you really want to help,

732
00:25:58,039 --> 00:25:59,200
help the oldest out more.

733
00:25:59,440 --> 00:26:00,079
I'll go get dinner.

734
00:26:00,759 --> 00:26:01,119
Dad!

735
00:26:02,400 --> 00:26:02,720
Dad!

736
00:26:04,319 --> 00:26:04,640
Dad!

737
00:26:05,119 --> 00:26:05,759
Listen to me,

738
00:26:06,160 --> 00:26:06,920
at the Ma family site,

739
00:26:07,119 --> 00:26:07,599
there's trouble!

740
00:26:08,559 --> 00:26:09,240
Here, let me take your coat.

741
00:26:09,240 --> 00:26:10,119
Haven't eaten yet? Waiting for me?

742
00:26:11,000 --> 00:26:12,119
Why'd you pinch me?

743
00:26:12,319 --> 00:26:12,880
Wait, something this big,

744
00:26:12,880 --> 00:26:13,920
I have to let Dad know!

745
00:26:14,319 --> 00:26:14,599
Dad,

746
00:26:15,079 --> 00:26:15,720
I'm telling you,

747
00:26:16,200 --> 00:26:17,039
that Ma family site...

748
00:26:17,400 --> 00:26:18,160
if nobody steps in,

749
00:26:18,319 --> 00:26:19,240
it's gonna blow up big time!

750
00:26:19,880 --> 00:26:22,039
Even the cops stormed over this afternoon!

751
00:26:22,279 --> 00:26:23,039
I really think

752
00:26:23,359 --> 00:26:24,240
the Ma family site

753
00:26:24,640 --> 00:26:26,359
needs someone sensible to take charge.

754
00:26:26,359 --> 00:26:27,720
There's trouble at our site!

755
00:26:27,720 --> 00:26:28,359
Did you know that?

756
00:26:30,200 --> 00:26:31,279
Our site?

757
00:26:32,000 --> 00:26:32,640
What happened?

758
00:26:34,720 --> 00:26:35,759
What happened at our site?

759
00:26:36,839 --> 00:26:37,160
I'm asking you!

760
00:26:40,319 --> 00:26:42,160
What... what happened at our site?

761
00:26:47,519 --> 00:26:47,839
Dad,

762
00:26:50,559 --> 00:26:51,559
what happened at our site?

763
00:26:51,920 --> 00:26:53,119
You're always late to the party.

764
00:26:53,880 --> 00:26:54,640
Good for nothing.

765
00:27:09,960 --> 00:27:11,440
You didn't see your dad when you went back.

766
00:27:13,240 --> 00:27:13,839
It's fine.

767
00:27:14,920 --> 00:27:16,640
Everyone needs time to process it.

768
00:27:17,400 --> 00:27:18,920
You need it, and so does he.

769
00:27:23,519 --> 00:27:25,079
Honey, I want to talk something over.

770
00:27:26,079 --> 00:27:27,119
About resigning right now...

771
00:27:28,039 --> 00:27:29,440
it won't get approved anytime soon.

772
00:27:30,119 --> 00:27:31,200
And over at Shi Yongnian's end,

773
00:27:32,000 --> 00:27:33,559
I don't think we'll land it quickly either.

774
00:27:34,240 --> 00:27:35,079
If this were before,

775
00:27:35,079 --> 00:27:36,359
back before my dad got sick,

776
00:27:37,559 --> 00:27:38,720
starting a firm, quitting my job...

777
00:27:39,160 --> 00:27:40,039
none of that would've been an issue.

778
00:27:40,279 --> 00:27:41,680
No matter how many times he slapped me,

779
00:27:41,680 --> 00:27:43,279
even if he disowned me,

780
00:27:44,039 --> 00:27:44,599
but right now,

781
00:27:45,160 --> 00:27:46,119
with his current condition,

782
00:27:47,319 --> 00:27:47,599
I...

783
00:27:48,200 --> 00:27:49,279
I really can't bring myself to do it.

784
00:27:49,960 --> 00:27:50,359
What if...

785
00:27:53,279 --> 00:27:53,799
the law firm...

786
00:27:54,519 --> 00:27:55,279
we put it on hold for now?

787
00:27:56,039 --> 00:27:56,519
What do you think?

788
00:27:57,200 --> 00:27:57,480
Wait,

789
00:27:59,480 --> 00:28:01,720
starting your firm and your dad's treatment—

790
00:28:02,480 --> 00:28:04,319
those two things don't conflict at all!

791
00:28:04,519 --> 00:28:05,400
I know they don't conflict,

792
00:28:05,519 --> 00:28:06,200
but don't you see?

793
00:28:06,200 --> 00:28:06,640
Right now,

794
00:28:07,720 --> 00:28:08,640
he won't even let me see him.

795
00:28:08,640 --> 00:28:10,119
How can I talk him into getting treatment?

796
00:28:10,519 --> 00:28:11,079
At least...

797
00:28:11,640 --> 00:28:12,880
if we pause it first, I...

798
00:28:13,359 --> 00:28:14,920
You think that'll make you feel better?

799
00:28:17,799 --> 00:28:18,559
But if you put it on hold,

800
00:28:19,839 --> 00:28:20,640
how much longer will you have to wait?

801
00:28:27,759 --> 00:28:28,400
I'm just afraid...

802
00:28:31,359 --> 00:28:32,640
I'm terrified of being blamed by everyone!

803
00:28:32,680 --> 00:28:33,440
If things go on like this,

804
00:28:34,480 --> 00:28:35,119
and the Sai family—

805
00:28:36,000 --> 00:28:37,240
from top to bottom,

806
00:28:38,240 --> 00:28:40,599
all they care about is money, money, money!

807
00:28:41,359 --> 00:28:42,680
Not one of them can step up and deliver.

808
00:28:44,279 --> 00:28:45,680
They're just screwing me over!

809
00:28:47,119 --> 00:28:48,279
The messier things get,

810
00:28:48,599 --> 00:28:49,599
the more we need to stay steady.

811
00:28:50,240 --> 00:28:51,599
Besides, a deal this big

812
00:28:52,200 --> 00:28:53,559
was never going to happen overnight.

813
00:28:54,039 --> 00:28:56,000
You've already taken the first step.

814
00:28:56,440 --> 00:28:58,039
How can you just pull back now?

815
00:28:58,559 --> 00:28:59,359
As for your dad,

816
00:29:00,200 --> 00:29:01,839
we'll figure out a way together.

817
00:29:03,400 --> 00:29:04,519
But your future...

818
00:29:05,039 --> 00:29:06,920
nothing should stand in the way of that.

819
00:29:38,880 --> 00:29:39,920
You two are crushing him!

820
00:29:40,039 --> 00:29:40,279
Dad.

821
00:29:40,359 --> 00:29:41,279
Get the wheelchair out, quick!

822
00:29:41,279 --> 00:29:41,839
Dad, Dad.

823
00:29:41,839 --> 00:29:42,359
Take it easy.

824
00:29:42,359 --> 00:29:43,039
Dad, take it slow.

825
00:29:43,319 --> 00:29:44,000
My legs won't cooperate.

826
00:29:44,599 --> 00:29:45,480
Don't push the wheelchair.

827
00:29:45,640 --> 00:29:46,599
Go around to that side. What are you doing?

828
00:29:46,799 --> 00:29:47,640
Why are you pushing it right here?

829
00:29:47,640 --> 00:29:48,160
You two, honestly...

830
00:29:48,160 --> 00:29:49,400
It's such a tight spot. Barely any room.

831
00:29:49,880 --> 00:29:50,480
Come on, easy does it.

832
00:29:50,480 --> 00:29:51,279
Turn around, turn around.

833
00:29:51,480 --> 00:29:52,400
Let me support you on this side.

834
00:29:53,480 --> 00:29:53,960
Sit down slowly.

835
00:29:54,839 --> 00:29:55,680
I'll help lift your legs up.

836
00:29:55,960 --> 00:29:56,319
Up you go.

837
00:29:57,119 --> 00:29:57,880
There we go.

838
00:29:58,680 --> 00:29:59,000
Dad.

839
00:29:59,519 --> 00:30:01,599
What are we actually doing here today?

840
00:30:01,880 --> 00:30:02,440
Yeah, Dad.

841
00:30:02,680 --> 00:30:03,880
Why didn't we go home after your discharge?

842
00:30:04,759 --> 00:30:06,920
All these sites of our Ma family...

843
00:30:07,759 --> 00:30:08,880
your mom and I,

844
00:30:09,559 --> 00:30:12,000
along with Uncle Xizi and Uncle Wei,

845
00:30:12,519 --> 00:30:13,480
one by one,

846
00:30:14,000 --> 00:30:14,720
fought tooth and nail to build them.

847
00:30:15,240 --> 00:30:15,920
Truth be told,

848
00:30:16,119 --> 00:30:16,960
without these sites,

849
00:30:17,400 --> 00:30:18,480
there'd be no family,

850
00:30:18,839 --> 00:30:20,160
and none of you.

851
00:30:21,799 --> 00:30:23,720
Lying in the hospital these days,

852
00:30:23,920 --> 00:30:24,880
I kept wondering to myself...

853
00:30:25,359 --> 00:30:26,599
Tell me, money...

854
00:30:27,119 --> 00:30:29,160
is it really a good thing after all?

855
00:30:30,640 --> 00:30:31,319
Over the years,

856
00:30:31,720 --> 00:30:34,599
our life has been getting better each day,

857
00:30:36,039 --> 00:30:38,240
so why does it feel emptier and emptier?

858
00:30:39,079 --> 00:30:40,079
Then I realized...

859
00:30:40,720 --> 00:30:41,839
it's not the money's fault.

860
00:30:42,519 --> 00:30:43,920
Maybe it's on me.

861
00:30:45,440 --> 00:30:46,640
Now I feel...

862
00:30:47,119 --> 00:30:49,480
like I've finally figured it out.

863
00:30:50,559 --> 00:30:50,960
Only...

864
00:30:51,400 --> 00:30:52,880
it seems a bit too late.

865
00:30:56,440 --> 00:30:56,839
Forget it.

866
00:30:57,960 --> 00:30:58,400
No point dwelling on it.

867
00:30:59,400 --> 00:31:00,640
Say, Auntie...

868
00:31:01,839 --> 00:31:02,400
Give it to them.

869
00:31:05,160 --> 00:31:06,039
So, we're dividing things up?

870
00:31:09,680 --> 00:31:10,720
I've made up my mind.

871
00:31:11,359 --> 00:31:11,960
The work site...

872
00:31:13,000 --> 00:31:13,640
...and the construction crew...

873
00:31:14,039 --> 00:31:15,000
...we can't split them up.

874
00:31:16,079 --> 00:31:17,000
For now,

875
00:31:17,000 --> 00:31:18,960
your aunt and Laijiao will run them.

876
00:31:20,079 --> 00:31:20,599
From now on,

877
00:31:20,599 --> 00:31:21,039
what my brother-in-law means is,

878
00:31:21,039 --> 00:31:21,920
whatever happens with the crew,

879
00:31:22,039 --> 00:31:22,720
if I'm not around,

880
00:31:22,960 --> 00:31:24,400
the two of them call the shots.

881
00:31:24,759 --> 00:31:25,119
Dad,

882
00:31:25,880 --> 00:31:27,000
what are you thinking?

883
00:31:27,559 --> 00:31:29,759
I get 300, and he gets 350?

884
00:31:30,000 --> 00:31:31,279
Why does he get more than me?

885
00:31:31,599 --> 00:31:32,680
You're playing favorites!

886
00:31:32,680 --> 00:31:33,839
You're lucky to get anything!

887
00:31:33,839 --> 00:31:34,920
How did you get less?

888
00:31:34,920 --> 00:31:35,839
You aren't even on the household registry!

889
00:31:35,920 --> 00:31:36,359
What do you want?

890
00:31:36,359 --> 00:31:37,039
So what if I'm not?

891
00:31:37,160 --> 00:31:38,359
You're married, but I'm not!

892
00:31:38,359 --> 00:31:38,759
Give it a rest!

893
00:31:38,759 --> 00:31:39,200
What are you yelling for?

894
00:31:39,200 --> 00:31:39,599
Alright!

895
00:31:39,599 --> 00:31:40,160
Stop fighting!

896
00:31:40,400 --> 00:31:40,759
That's enough!

897
00:31:41,200 --> 00:31:42,480
Let your dad finish talking!

898
00:31:43,640 --> 00:31:46,519
We didn't come here to talk business today.

899
00:31:46,720 --> 00:31:48,440
We're here to speak from the heart

900
00:31:48,599 --> 00:31:49,880
and leave something to remember.

901
00:31:49,880 --> 00:31:50,400
Exactly.

902
00:31:50,880 --> 00:31:51,799
Whether you're happy or not,

903
00:31:51,960 --> 00:31:53,039
th-this is it.

904
00:31:53,680 --> 00:31:54,640
Dacheng, Dacheng...

905
00:31:55,359 --> 00:31:57,119
Today wraps it all up nicely.

906
00:31:57,480 --> 00:31:58,960
The building is finished now,

907
00:31:59,920 --> 00:32:00,359
and the family affairs...

908
00:32:00,680 --> 00:32:01,640
...are settled once and for all.

909
00:32:01,880 --> 00:32:02,319
Going forward,

910
00:32:02,720 --> 00:32:03,720
let's all look ahead.

911
00:32:03,720 --> 00:32:05,279
Exactly. What an asshole my brother is.

912
00:32:05,279 --> 00:32:05,640
Dad!

913
00:32:06,200 --> 00:32:06,759
Same as usual,

914
00:32:07,160 --> 00:32:08,960
let's take a photo with the building.

915
00:32:09,039 --> 00:32:09,799
Let's take a photo, Dad.

916
00:32:10,079 --> 00:32:10,559
Go on, go.

917
00:32:10,759 --> 00:32:11,359
I called them over!

918
00:32:11,759 --> 00:32:12,079
Bro!

919
00:32:12,079 --> 00:32:12,720
Time for a photo, boys!

920
00:32:12,720 --> 00:32:13,279
Big Brother!

921
00:32:13,279 --> 00:32:14,960
Dad, he took the money and left.

922
00:32:15,400 --> 00:32:16,240
What an ungrateful bastard.

923
00:32:16,440 --> 00:32:16,880
Don't worry.

924
00:32:16,880 --> 00:32:17,480
You still have me.

925
00:32:17,559 --> 00:32:18,839
I'll always take good care of you.

926
00:32:18,880 --> 00:32:20,799
And so, the Ma family's money was split.

927
00:32:22,119 --> 00:32:23,680
Life had to go on.

928
00:32:25,640 --> 00:32:26,880
But Old Ma ended up paralyzed,

929
00:32:27,680 --> 00:32:28,839
the brothers turned on each other,

930
00:32:29,960 --> 00:32:30,960
and after all that fighting...

931
00:32:31,920 --> 00:32:32,920
...who really won?

932
00:32:37,079 --> 00:32:37,440
President Shi.

933
00:32:37,839 --> 00:32:38,440
Mr. Wei is here.

934
00:32:41,519 --> 00:32:41,839
Have a seat.

935
00:32:42,599 --> 00:32:43,519
Try this new tea of mine.

936
00:32:51,200 --> 00:32:51,720
Well...

937
00:32:52,920 --> 00:32:53,480
Mr. Shi...

938
00:32:54,440 --> 00:32:55,720
I came here today

939
00:32:56,039 --> 00:32:58,000
regarding that sea sand issue.

940
00:32:58,720 --> 00:32:59,799
That site supervisor...

941
00:32:59,799 --> 00:33:02,160
was sent to the police for investigation.

942
00:33:03,119 --> 00:33:04,839
It really was our fault,

943
00:33:05,319 --> 00:33:06,319
delaying the project schedule

944
00:33:06,599 --> 00:33:08,720
and causing you and Tengyue so much trouble.

945
00:33:09,160 --> 00:33:10,240
I feel terribly guilty.

946
00:33:11,880 --> 00:33:13,480
Reprimand or fine us as you see fit—

947
00:33:13,559 --> 00:33:14,240
we'll take full responsibility.

948
00:33:14,920 --> 00:33:16,160
The last time we met,

949
00:33:16,319 --> 00:33:17,480
didn't I warn you?

950
00:33:18,400 --> 00:33:19,240
You did, you did.

951
00:33:21,000 --> 00:33:22,720
Fortunately, it was caught in time,

952
00:33:22,720 --> 00:33:24,079
and all of that sea sand

953
00:33:24,359 --> 00:33:25,480
has been completely cleared out.

954
00:33:25,920 --> 00:33:26,920
I've worked on construction sites.

955
00:33:27,799 --> 00:33:29,039
Nothing on a site is a small matter.

956
00:33:30,079 --> 00:33:31,079
It was caught early this time.

957
00:33:31,920 --> 00:33:32,880
If it had actually been mixed in,

958
00:33:33,640 --> 00:33:34,839
the consequences would be catastrophic.

959
00:33:35,799 --> 00:33:36,559
I know, I know.

960
00:33:37,200 --> 00:33:37,720
Mr. Shi...

961
00:33:38,519 --> 00:33:40,240
I promise there won't be a next—

962
00:33:41,119 --> 00:33:42,079
How can you guarantee that?

963
00:33:49,920 --> 00:33:50,640
Some things...

964
00:33:51,799 --> 00:33:52,960
need to be solved at the root.

965
00:33:55,000 --> 00:33:55,920
I have an idea.

966
00:33:56,480 --> 00:33:57,279
Want to hear it?

967
00:33:58,079 --> 00:33:58,480
Go ahead.

968
00:34:01,240 --> 00:34:02,359
Have you ever considered...

969
00:34:02,799 --> 00:34:03,839
selling your company?

970
00:34:10,960 --> 00:34:11,679
What do you mean?

971
00:34:11,920 --> 00:34:12,400
Are you saying...

972
00:34:12,400 --> 00:34:13,760
you want to buy me out?

973
00:34:15,280 --> 00:34:15,760
Dacheng...

974
00:34:16,639 --> 00:34:17,920
Let me show you something.

975
00:34:20,760 --> 00:34:21,039
Here.

976
00:34:31,719 --> 00:34:33,239
I'm not much better off than you.

977
00:34:33,920 --> 00:34:34,239
Have you...

978
00:34:35,639 --> 00:34:36,960
have you told your family yet?

979
00:34:37,280 --> 00:34:38,280
What's there to say?

980
00:34:39,880 --> 00:34:41,159
You've got three kids,

981
00:34:41,159 --> 00:34:42,280
and look at the mess they're making.

982
00:34:42,599 --> 00:34:44,039
I've got five.

983
00:34:44,880 --> 00:34:46,280
I can't afford that kind of shame.

984
00:34:49,320 --> 00:34:50,920
So... what did the doctor say?

985
00:34:51,440 --> 00:34:52,719
Isn't it the same old line?

986
00:34:53,760 --> 00:34:54,119
You know,

987
00:34:55,000 --> 00:34:56,119
a fifty-fifty chance.

988
00:34:57,119 --> 00:34:59,440
Isn't that what they always say?

989
00:35:02,199 --> 00:35:03,199
Brother Wei, listen to me.

990
00:35:05,679 --> 00:35:06,760
Ever since I came to Honggang,

991
00:35:07,960 --> 00:35:08,800
my team

992
00:35:09,000 --> 00:35:10,079
has done some research.

993
00:35:10,679 --> 00:35:11,920
We found that Changfu

994
00:35:12,079 --> 00:35:14,119
really is a solid company.

995
00:35:14,719 --> 00:35:15,760
In the construction industry today,

996
00:35:15,760 --> 00:35:16,280
as you know,

997
00:35:16,880 --> 00:35:18,199
it's not like back in our day.

998
00:35:18,320 --> 00:35:19,039
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

999
00:35:19,039 --> 00:35:20,960
Just relying on muscle and loyalty

1000
00:35:21,119 --> 00:35:21,880
was enough to get by.

1001
00:35:22,159 --> 00:35:23,800
Competition is fierce now.

1002
00:35:25,039 --> 00:35:27,320
Crews must standardize safety regulations.

1003
00:35:27,880 --> 00:35:29,760
If Changfu keeps dragging on like this,

1004
00:35:30,280 --> 00:35:31,400
it's not going to work.

1005
00:35:33,639 --> 00:35:36,159
But you're asking me to sell the company.

1006
00:35:36,360 --> 00:35:38,079
What about my men?

1007
00:35:39,000 --> 00:35:41,000
Brother Xi, Brother Ma...

1008
00:35:41,639 --> 00:35:42,920
they all count on me for work.

1009
00:35:43,280 --> 00:35:44,000
If I sell,

1010
00:35:44,280 --> 00:35:46,000
wouldn't I cut off their livelihood?

1011
00:35:49,079 --> 00:35:49,719
Mr. Shi...

1012
00:35:49,880 --> 00:35:51,960
Do you really just want to buy me out?

1013
00:35:53,760 --> 00:35:55,760
Since you old buddies can't play bad cop,

1014
00:35:56,280 --> 00:35:56,880
and management has slipped,

1015
00:35:57,320 --> 00:35:58,400
why not take the simple way out?

1016
00:35:58,719 --> 00:35:59,239
Besides,

1017
00:35:59,639 --> 00:36:00,519
real estate lasts a hundred years,

1018
00:36:00,920 --> 00:36:01,800
but construction lasts forever.

1019
00:36:02,199 --> 00:36:03,679
Real estate is cyclical,

1020
00:36:04,000 --> 00:36:05,280
but construction is eternal.

1021
00:36:06,599 --> 00:36:08,599
If Tengyue wants to grow stronger,

1022
00:36:08,719 --> 00:36:10,679
acquiring Changfu is the only path forward.

1023
00:36:11,639 --> 00:36:13,519
I'm being completely sincere.

1024
00:36:14,440 --> 00:36:15,360
Brother Wei, think about it.

1025
00:36:15,800 --> 00:36:18,079
If the two of us can pull this off,

1026
00:36:19,119 --> 00:36:20,119
Tengyue's capital,

1027
00:36:20,599 --> 00:36:21,800
management, and projects

1028
00:36:22,239 --> 00:36:23,800
can all be poured into Changfu.

1029
00:36:23,920 --> 00:36:24,880
Overnight,

1030
00:36:25,480 --> 00:36:26,920
Changfu will be transformed

1031
00:36:27,159 --> 00:36:28,239
and taken to the next level.

1032
00:36:28,440 --> 00:36:29,440
As for those outdated crews

1033
00:36:29,599 --> 00:36:31,400
with no quality control,

1034
00:36:31,599 --> 00:36:32,400
I'll deal with them for you.

1035
00:36:32,719 --> 00:36:35,119
Everyone wins.

1036
00:36:35,880 --> 00:36:36,679
It's a win-win.

1037
00:36:40,880 --> 00:36:41,280
Well...

1038
00:36:43,119 --> 00:36:44,000
Brother Wei,

1039
00:36:45,840 --> 00:36:46,519
there's no rush

1040
00:36:47,559 --> 00:36:48,119
on this.

1041
00:36:49,400 --> 00:36:49,840
Why don't you

1042
00:36:50,239 --> 00:36:51,239
take your time and think it over?

1043
00:36:52,239 --> 00:36:52,760
Either way,

1044
00:36:53,079 --> 00:36:54,039
whatever you decide,

1045
00:36:57,000 --> 00:36:57,559
I'll respect it.

1046
00:37:08,320 --> 00:37:09,079
Well,

1047
00:37:13,119 --> 00:37:13,400
by the way...

1048
00:37:13,880 --> 00:37:14,639
I still remember,

1049
00:37:15,159 --> 00:37:15,800
when we were kids,

1050
00:37:16,719 --> 00:37:17,920
our family never had enough meat.

1051
00:37:18,079 --> 00:37:19,719
Your dad would call me and my brother over

1052
00:37:19,719 --> 00:37:21,639
to your place to gnaw on pork trotters.

1053
00:37:21,639 --> 00:37:22,239
Remember that?

1054
00:37:22,760 --> 00:37:23,639
A-And another time,

1055
00:37:23,920 --> 00:37:24,599
it made, uh...

1056
00:37:24,960 --> 00:37:25,320
your brother

1057
00:37:25,880 --> 00:37:27,000
get so frantic, he burst into tears.

1058
00:37:27,559 --> 00:37:28,320
Do you remember?

1059
00:37:30,639 --> 00:37:32,119
Childhood really was the best.

1060
00:37:33,639 --> 00:37:34,360
We were totally carefree.

1061
00:37:39,320 --> 00:37:40,159
If anything happens down the road,

1062
00:37:41,119 --> 00:37:42,000
don't shoulder it all on your own.

1063
00:37:42,880 --> 00:37:43,800
To care for your dad,

1064
00:37:44,119 --> 00:37:45,559
you've got to take care of yourself first.

1065
00:37:45,760 --> 00:37:46,880
Only then can he have someone to lean on.

1066
00:37:47,199 --> 00:37:48,400
The more your dad depends on you,

1067
00:37:48,800 --> 00:37:49,679
you've got to treat yourself

1068
00:37:50,000 --> 00:37:50,639
even better.

1069
00:38:01,119 --> 00:38:01,960
That construction team...

1070
00:38:02,480 --> 00:38:04,360
is the only lifeline I have left.

1071
00:38:06,159 --> 00:38:07,360
We've got to find a way.

1072
00:38:08,880 --> 00:38:10,079
Before I got this illness,

1073
00:38:10,599 --> 00:38:11,840
I had such big ambitions.

1074
00:38:12,840 --> 00:38:14,599
14 million!

1075
00:38:14,639 --> 00:38:15,159
Yeah.

1076
00:38:15,360 --> 00:38:16,880
I didn't want just scraps anymore.

1077
00:38:17,440 --> 00:38:18,320
I wanted real meat.

1078
00:38:18,800 --> 00:38:19,960
I was going to start a company.

1079
00:38:20,320 --> 00:38:22,519
I was going to be Old Wei's equal.

1080
00:38:23,920 --> 00:38:24,880
Now look at things.

1081
00:38:25,599 --> 00:38:27,039
You just divided up the money,

1082
00:38:27,400 --> 00:38:28,079
nice and easy.

1083
00:38:29,039 --> 00:38:30,440
But what am I supposed to do?

1084
00:38:30,599 --> 00:38:31,880
I haven't figured it out yet!

1085
00:38:33,159 --> 00:38:33,599
Xizi,

1086
00:38:34,159 --> 00:38:35,599
have a proper talk with the kids.

1087
00:38:35,800 --> 00:38:36,880
There has to be a way.

1088
00:38:36,960 --> 00:38:38,599
Don't you still have your eldest?

1089
00:38:38,599 --> 00:38:39,360
Well... No, no, no.

1090
00:38:39,920 --> 00:38:40,920
The eldest can't cut it.

1091
00:38:41,039 --> 00:38:42,320
He has no backbone.

1092
00:38:42,960 --> 00:38:44,280
He can't shoulder responsibility.

1093
00:38:44,679 --> 00:38:46,159
Then you still have your second son.

1094
00:38:53,480 --> 00:38:56,599
If only the two could be rolled into one!

1095
00:38:58,760 --> 00:39:00,000
As long as the brothers unite,

1096
00:39:00,719 --> 00:39:01,360
and this family

1097
00:39:01,840 --> 00:39:02,920
doesn't fall apart, that's enough.

1098
00:39:28,400 --> 00:39:29,559
Take this.

1099
00:39:32,480 --> 00:39:33,239
What is this?

1100
00:39:33,840 --> 00:39:35,239
The address of your brother's law firm.

1101
00:39:35,559 --> 00:39:37,679
Go over and see what's going on.

1102
00:39:38,039 --> 00:39:38,920
Have a good talk with him.

1103
00:39:39,239 --> 00:39:40,760
Me? Talk to him...

1104
00:39:41,280 --> 00:39:42,119
about what, Dad?

1105
00:39:42,480 --> 00:39:43,400
Just tell him,

1106
00:39:43,800 --> 00:39:45,320
as long as he goes back to work,

1107
00:39:46,000 --> 00:39:47,239
I'll give him whatever he asks for.

1108
00:39:47,280 --> 00:39:47,960
Tell him to name a figure.

1109
00:39:48,880 --> 00:39:49,199
Also,

1110
00:39:50,199 --> 00:39:52,119
tell him and Meifan to have a baby soon.

1111
00:39:52,559 --> 00:39:53,679
If they need money,

1112
00:39:54,079 --> 00:39:54,519
I'll pay.

1113
00:39:55,320 --> 00:39:56,239
Even if I go talk to him,

1114
00:39:56,239 --> 00:39:58,480
he... he might not listen to me, Dad.

1115
00:39:58,599 --> 00:40:00,000
Just talk to him nicely.

1116
00:40:00,280 --> 00:40:01,239
He'll listen.

1117
00:40:10,400 --> 00:40:10,840
Hey, buddy,

1118
00:40:11,239 --> 00:40:12,320
that table over there,

1119
00:40:12,320 --> 00:40:13,519
could you help me put it down in a bit?

1120
00:40:16,840 --> 00:40:17,559
You're just in time.

1121
00:40:17,880 --> 00:40:19,880
Boss, our breaker keeps tripping.

1122
00:40:19,880 --> 00:40:20,559
What's going on?

1123
00:40:20,960 --> 00:40:21,679
The breaker keeps tripping?

1124
00:40:21,840 --> 00:40:22,199
Yeah.

1125
00:40:22,639 --> 00:40:23,320
Where's your breaker box?

1126
00:40:23,760 --> 00:40:24,039
Over there.

1127
00:40:29,400 --> 00:40:30,320
Most likely,

1128
00:40:30,559 --> 00:40:33,000
the wire gauge isn't thick enough.

1129
00:40:33,960 --> 00:40:34,880
So whenever you use

1130
00:40:35,079 --> 00:40:36,480
high-power appliances, it's bound to trip.

1131
00:40:37,119 --> 00:40:39,519
You'll just have to rewire it.

1132
00:40:39,840 --> 00:40:41,039
Rewire?

1133
00:40:42,159 --> 00:40:43,480
I already paid you the final balance!

1134
00:40:43,480 --> 00:40:44,679
And now you're telling me to rewire?

1135
00:40:45,360 --> 00:40:46,719
You're trying to rip me off, aren't you?

1136
00:40:46,880 --> 00:40:48,000
You have to fix it for me today!

1137
00:40:48,119 --> 00:40:48,920
If you don't fix it,

1138
00:40:48,920 --> 00:40:49,519
we'll sue you.

1139
00:40:49,599 --> 00:40:50,119
We'll sue until you pay us back!

1140
00:40:50,119 --> 00:40:50,800
What's all the shouting about?

1141
00:40:50,920 --> 00:40:51,320
I—

1142
00:40:51,800 --> 00:40:52,159
Big Brother!

1143
00:40:52,960 --> 00:40:54,440
Boss, this guy is picking on us!

1144
00:40:54,559 --> 00:40:55,519
Not only did he mess up the breaker,

1145
00:40:55,519 --> 00:40:56,559
he's also telling us to rewire

1146
00:40:56,679 --> 00:40:57,119
just to shake us down for money!

1147
00:40:57,119 --> 00:40:58,159
What kind of nonsense is this?

1148
00:40:58,159 --> 00:41:00,079
He and this big brother aren't the same.

1149
00:41:00,280 --> 00:41:01,079
This is my real older brother.

1150
00:41:01,679 --> 00:41:02,400
And this is my younger brother.

1151
00:41:03,800 --> 00:41:04,320
Hello, Big Brother.

1152
00:41:04,800 --> 00:41:05,320
Let's talk inside.

1153
00:41:08,039 --> 00:41:08,840
Sorry about that, Big Brother.

1154
00:41:08,840 --> 00:41:09,159
It's fine.

1155
00:41:09,719 --> 00:41:10,639
Later, I'll find someone

1156
00:41:11,039 --> 00:41:11,679
to get it sorted out for you.

1157
00:41:12,039 --> 00:41:12,360
In this room...

1158
00:41:20,440 --> 00:41:20,800
Have a seat.

1159
00:41:23,119 --> 00:41:24,679
Do you still see me as your brother?

1160
00:41:24,920 --> 00:41:25,880
With this renovation,

1161
00:41:26,119 --> 00:41:27,119
if you'd just told me,

1162
00:41:27,920 --> 00:41:29,000
think how much money I could've saved you.

1163
00:41:30,280 --> 00:41:32,159
You got ripped off just now, right?

1164
00:41:33,039 --> 00:41:33,639
You don't even have...

1165
00:41:34,000 --> 00:41:36,280
They didn't even install standard breakers.

1166
00:41:36,880 --> 00:41:37,760
How's Dad doing?

1167
00:41:38,079 --> 00:41:38,519
He's doing well.

1168
00:41:39,079 --> 00:41:39,639
No, look...

1169
00:41:39,679 --> 00:41:41,559
Don't just say he's doing well.

1170
00:41:42,519 --> 00:41:43,719
You—keep a close eye on him.

1171
00:41:43,719 --> 00:41:44,599
Don't let him overwork himself.

1172
00:41:45,199 --> 00:41:45,760
With his health...

1173
00:41:47,440 --> 00:41:47,679
He...

1174
00:41:48,400 --> 00:41:49,639
Let's put it this way:

1175
00:41:50,519 --> 00:41:51,559
when you're young,

1176
00:41:51,559 --> 00:41:52,239
your body can take anything.

1177
00:41:52,440 --> 00:41:53,800
But once you get up there in age,

1178
00:41:54,400 --> 00:41:55,880
sometimes you seem totally fine,

1179
00:41:56,079 --> 00:41:57,199
and then you just collapse out of nowhere.

1180
00:41:58,639 --> 00:42:00,039
You make it sound like we don't care.

1181
00:42:00,039 --> 00:42:00,400
Right?

1182
00:42:00,800 --> 00:42:01,719
As if we at home...

1183
00:42:01,920 --> 00:42:03,159
are just totally useless.

1184
00:42:03,199 --> 00:42:05,360
Isn't it 'cause you're close and I'm far?

1185
00:42:05,599 --> 00:42:06,760
Tell me, aside from you,

1186
00:42:06,760 --> 00:42:07,960
who else can I count on? Name one.

1187
00:42:08,119 --> 00:42:08,719
Who else?

1188
00:42:15,280 --> 00:42:16,400
Bro, it's true...

1189
00:42:17,079 --> 00:42:17,920
About me quitting my job,

1190
00:42:18,920 --> 00:42:19,840
not telling you guys beforehand

1191
00:42:19,840 --> 00:42:20,519
was my fault.

1192
00:42:21,400 --> 00:42:23,239
But didn't your wife go a bit too far?

1193
00:42:25,599 --> 00:42:25,800
Look...

1194
00:42:26,440 --> 00:42:27,480
The things she said that day...

1195
00:42:27,960 --> 00:42:29,360
has she ever apologized to me?

1196
00:42:29,719 --> 00:42:30,519
To this day,

1197
00:42:30,519 --> 00:42:32,159
has she ever said a single "sorry" to me?

1198
00:42:33,159 --> 00:42:34,320
If I said I didn't resent it,

1199
00:42:34,320 --> 00:42:35,079
that'd be a lie.

1200
00:42:35,960 --> 00:42:37,599
But she's your wife.

1201
00:42:38,719 --> 00:42:39,719
Right now, I can't even tell

1202
00:42:39,719 --> 00:42:40,480
if, before she said those things,

1203
00:42:40,480 --> 00:42:41,159
she discussed it with you first.

1204
00:42:41,519 --> 00:42:41,760
No...

1205
00:42:42,239 --> 00:42:42,840
I had nothing to do with it!

1206
00:42:43,000 --> 00:42:44,920
Not me. I really had no clue!

1207
00:42:46,079 --> 00:42:46,679
I believe you.

1208
00:42:47,440 --> 00:42:48,719
Because we're real brothers,

1209
00:42:49,400 --> 00:42:50,480
and the fact you came here today

1210
00:42:51,199 --> 00:42:51,920
shows your good intentions.

1211
00:42:52,639 --> 00:42:53,159
I accept it.

1212
00:42:53,800 --> 00:42:54,920
Let's consider this matter closed.

1213
00:42:55,400 --> 00:42:56,000
We won't bring it up again.

1214
00:43:00,559 --> 00:43:01,239
So...

1215
00:43:04,000 --> 00:43:05,280
go back to work at the Port Authority.

1216
00:43:10,559 --> 00:43:11,719
Is that what you came here for?

1217
00:43:20,119 --> 00:43:21,000
Eldest Brother, do you think

1218
00:43:21,000 --> 00:43:22,119
your wife forced you into this?

1219
00:43:22,119 --> 00:43:23,719
Does every wife in the world

1220
00:43:23,719 --> 00:43:24,800
have to pressure her husband?

1221
00:43:25,039 --> 00:43:25,920
I just don't get it.

1222
00:43:26,039 --> 00:43:27,199
Quitting to work at a law firm—

1223
00:43:27,199 --> 00:43:28,280
what's so wrong with that?

1224
00:43:28,280 --> 00:43:29,519
You broke Dad's heart.

1225
00:43:29,599 --> 00:43:30,880
Well, mine's broken too!

1226
00:43:31,639 --> 00:43:32,480
Urology?

1227
00:43:33,559 --> 00:43:34,480
What does it say on here?

1228
00:43:34,480 --> 00:43:34,840
What about it?

1229
00:43:35,079 --> 00:43:36,039
When I did the laundry,

1230
00:43:36,039 --> 00:43:37,639
I found it in the washing machine.

1231
00:43:38,159 --> 00:43:38,960
I'm not even dating anyone.

1232
00:43:39,559 --> 00:43:40,599
We share a bed every night.

1233
00:43:40,599 --> 00:43:41,159
You know my situation,

1234
00:43:41,159 --> 00:43:41,960
don't you?

1235
00:43:41,960 --> 00:43:43,159
Then that only leaves Xiao Wu.
